nodes.body:
The one thing worth deciding before anyone reviews this in depth: #40608 reworks HiCache host-pool assembly around declarations, and this PR's only dispatch change is a branch inside `get_mha_host_pool_cls` (`pool_host/mha.py`). Those two rebase cleanly against current `main` — I re-checked after rebasing onto `4407a21f3c` — but if the declaration mechanism is meant to subsume per-class dispatch, this should become a declaration rather than a branch, and I would rather reshape it now than after review.

@ispobock is #40608 expected to land first, and would you like the INT8 pool expressed as a declaration on top of it? If so I am happy to hold this and rework against that PR. If not, the current shape stands on its own and is ready for review.

Separately, the rebase in this push also clears the two real `Lint` failures from the previous head (a `ruff format` diff and a missing `register_cpu_ci` in the codec test); `Lint` is green on the current head. A fork cannot apply the `run-ci` label, so the two new test files still have not executed in CI — a `/tag-and-rerun-ci` would start them.

